From d4c4eb64036d1329998e6bec725ba79d1273effd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:10:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 217/219] [EXTERNALLY-MAINTAINED] hid-asus-ally: restore the
 gamepad mode on resume

On the ROG Xbox Ally X20 (RC74XA, MCU firmware RC74XA.322), the MCU
sometimes comes back from s2idle in its default desktop mode: the sticks
drive the N-Key mouse interface, the gamepad reports are all neutral and
the QAM buttons arrive as F1/F8 instead of vendor reports. The USB
device is neither reset nor re-enumerated, so reset_resume and a reprobe
never run, and gamepad_mode still reads back the cached value.

Runtime-suspending the MCU and then evaluating Display Off followed by
Sleep Entry on \_SB.PEP, the order s2idle uses, reproduced the mode loss
in about half of the attempts. It was not observed with the USB link
active, and setting mcu_powersave to 0 did not avoid it. Repeating the
sequence with the link active restored gamepad mode, which may explain
why a second suspend usually fixes the issue.

The resume path already re-applies the button mapping, deadzones and
response curves through _gamepad_apply_all(), but never the mode
itself. Send the recorded mode with _gamepad_set_mode() instead, which
then re-applies the same settings.

With this change, 6 out of 6 attempts of the reproducer came back in
gamepad mode, 3 of which were in desktop mode until the mode was
restored.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
index 657ad2cb831a..0dbf6d28caf4 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-asus-ally.c
@@ -2245,7 +2245,11 @@ static int ally_hid_resume(struct hid_device *hdev)
 	if (!ally_cfg || ep != ROG_ALLY_CFG_INTF_IN)
 		return 0;
 
-	err = _gamepad_apply_all(hdev, ally_cfg);
+	/*
+	 * The MCU can lose its mode across s2idle without a USB reset.
+	 * Restore the cached mode and reapply the mappings and axis settings.
+	 */
+	err = _gamepad_set_mode(hdev, ally_cfg, ally_cfg->mode);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
